GAL22V10
UA6RH800

AB1 AB2 AB3 AB4 AB5 AB6 GALSTB RCFG8 RCFG4 RCFG2 BASEA GND
RW CFGIN NC15 ACPHASE RST DB15 DB14 DB13 DB12 NC22 DRVEN VCC

; =================================================================
; UA6 - RocHard RH800C  (first-principles rebuild)
; Model: "er_Type override + /_DRVEN enable"  (see ua6-rebuild-spec)
; Memory base is FIXED $200000 (per card docs) -> NO base latch here.
;
; UA6 does exactly two jobs:
;   1) /DRVEN  - master autoconfig enable for UA4 (without it UA4 cannot
;                produce /_E8WIN or drive config data -> NO autoconfig).
;   2) Override the single board's er_Type MEMLIST+SIZE bits on DB12-15,
;      from the RAM straps: ROM's static 0xC0 (controller, no memory) ->
;      0xE0 / 0xE7 / 0xE6 (controller + 8/4/2 MB memory) when RAM fitted.
;   The ROM supplies every OTHER autoconfig register (mfr 2144, product..).
;
; Signal senses (net level):
;   /GALSTB (p7, from UA4 o21) = LOW when "$E8 autoconfig access AND a RAM
;       strap is set" -> already means RAM-present, so it also gates size.
;   /CFGIN  (p14) = LOW = our turn in the autoconfig chain
;   /RST    (p17) = LOW = system reset ; RST (high) = not-reset
;   /RCFG8/4/2 (p8/9/10) = LOW = that size selected (one at a time)
;   RW (p13) = 1 read / 0 write ;  AB1..AB6 = config-space offset A1..A6
; =================================================================


; ---- /DRVEN : enable UA4's autoconfig drivers during our access --------
; Assert (LOW) on our turn + autoconfig access (/GALSTB) + not reset,
; with a self-hold so it survives the UA4 /_GALSTROBE <-> /DRVEN handshake.
; BENCH TODO: confirm hold-vs-pulse timing of this handshake on real HW.
/DRVEN = /CFGIN & /GALSTB & RST
       + /CFGIN & /DRVEN  & RST


; ---- er_Type nibble on DB12-15 (only driven during our er_Type read) ---
; er_Type hi nibble @0x00 (A1=0): 0xE = 1110 -> D15=1 D14=1 D13=1 D12=0
;                                             (D13=1 sets ERTF_MEMLIST)
; er_Type lo nibble @0x02 (A1=1) = SIZE code on D14 D13 D12:
;     8MB=000  4MB=111  2MB=110      (D15=0 in lo nibble)
;   DB12 = 1 only for 4MB              (RCFG4 asserted)
;   DB13 = DB14 = 1 for hi-nibble(memlist) OR lo-nibble 4MB/2MB
DB15.T = /AB1
DB14.T = /AB1 + AB1 & /RCFG4 + AB1 & /RCFG2
DB13.T = /AB1 + AB1 & /RCFG4 + AB1 & /RCFG2
DB12.T =        AB1 & /RCFG4

; Tri-state enable (single product term): drive only when it is OUR
; autoconfig READ of the er_Type register.  /GALSTB already implies
; "$E8 access AND RAM present", so no-RAM => /GALSTB idle => Hi-Z =>
; er_Type stays the ROM's 0xC0 (memlist clear => no memory added).
; er_Type register = offset 0x00/0x02 => A2..A6 = 0.
DB15.E = /CFGIN & /GALSTB & RW & RST & /AB2 & /AB3 & /AB4 & /AB5 & /AB6
DB14.E = /CFGIN & /GALSTB & RW & RST & /AB2 & /AB3 & /AB4 & /AB5 & /AB6
DB13.E = /CFGIN & /GALSTB & RW & RST & /AB2 & /AB3 & /AB4 & /AB5 & /AB6
DB12.E = /CFGIN & /GALSTB & RW & RST & /AB2 & /AB3 & /AB4 & /AB5 & /AB6


; ---- ACPHASE (p16 -> U11 p5) : unused by U11's crack; left undriven ----
; NC15 (p15), NC22 (p22): unconnected pads on the PCB; left undriven.


DESCRIPTION

UA6 rebuild for RocHard RH800C, derived from the Zorro II autoconfig spec +
WinUAE + the neighbour GAL equations (the original UA6 could not be read).

WHAT IT DOES
  - /DRVEN gates UA4's autoconfig response (master enable).
  - Overrides er_Type MEMLIST + SIZE from the RAMCFG straps so the OS adds
    2/4/8 MB of fast RAM at the fixed $200000 base. No RAM strap => no drive
    => board reports as controller-only (matches WinUAE's static ROM view).

KNOWN OPEN ITEMS (resolve on the bench, this is a FIRST test burn)
  1. Bus arbitration: this assumes the ROM is NOT driving DB12-15 during $E8
     autoconfig reads (so UA6 owns er_Type). If the ROM does drive there,
     expect contention on D13/size bits -> re-gate or disable ROM in $E8.
  2. /GALSTB <-> /DRVEN async handshake: verify the self-hold behaves
     (no chatter, releases correctly). Scope UA6 p23 during boot autoconfig.
  3. /_AC_PHASE (p16) left undriven - confirm nothing on the card needs it.
  4. Strap polarity assumed active-low (/RCFG*), one selected at a time,
     per UA4's equations.

TEST: burn, install with the other ORIGINAL chips, boot the Amiga, check the
memory list / 'avail' for the 2/4/8 MB and whether the card now autoconfigs.
